    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0485" n="1553" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p2/pg1553"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">110.11 DU/2–153</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the President </hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d265-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-02-01">February 1,
                        1953</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>:] Stassen and I met in Rome
                    with De Gasperi and his principal Ministers, notably Defense Minister Pacciardi
                    and Finance Minister Pella. We had a talk alone with De Gasperi.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d265-f2"/> Your personal letter<anchor n="3" xml:id="d265-f3"/>
                    greatly appreciated and very helpful. Believe these meetings constructive in
                    lending our support to very evident desire Italian Government to advance
                    European unity. Their need for financial assistance appears moderate and based
                    on realistic study their needs. We also discussed possible solution Trieste
                    problem and will pursue this matter further. Entire visit in most cordial
                    official and public atmosphere.</p>
                <p>[Best regards,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Foster</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d265-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d265-f1-content">
                <p>This message was transmitted to the Department of State in telegram 4274 from
                    Paris, Feb. 1, with instructions that it be forwarded to the President and that
                    there be no distribution except for Acting Secretary Matthews.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d265-f2" n="2" xml:id="d265-f2-content">
                <p>For a record of Dulles’ and Stassen’s meetings with De Gasperi and other leading
                    government officials, see telegram 4275 from Paris, Feb. 1, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d265-f3" n="3" xml:id="d265-f3-content">
                <p>Concerning Eisenhower’s letter to De Gasperi, see footnote 7, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
